WEBVTT

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:28.760
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:28.760
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:28.760
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:53.160 --> 00:02:02.460
Chapter II

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:12.020
On September 19th of Space Year 788,
Yang Wenli was appointed Lieutenant at 10:25...

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:17.710
...and then became a Lieutenant
Commander at 16:30 at the age of 21.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:22.160
It is a bizarre arrangement
born out of the unwritten law...

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:25.690
...that a double promotion cannot
be awarded to someone still living.

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:29.550
But still, his tenure of only six hours as a
Lieutenant set a record for the fastest promotion...

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:32.930
...in the history of the Free Planets Alliance
Defense Force since its establishment.

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:42.560
I hope you'll work hard so you can break the
fastest promotion record for Commander, too.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:43.810
Good luck.

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:44.860
Y...yes.

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:47.130
Of course,
you can smile.

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:48.750
It's not you who'll
have to work hard.

00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:57.890
Having rescued 3,000,000 civilians from
El Facil, Yang was turned into a hero overnight.

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:05.310
But the more he was lionized by the people
around him, the more cynical he became.

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:07.500
But, Lt. Commander...

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:11.890
...you're a fortunate man.

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:16.270
To become a Lt. Commander at the age of 21,
you must have been born under a lucky star.

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:23.630
When the founder of the Free Planets
Alliance, Ale Heinessen, was 21 years old...

00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:28.400
...he was conscripted to hard labor
at an arctic deportation settlement.

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:34.160
Considering such a predicament, your
present situation is quite a privileged one.

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:41.260
As you understand the struggles of our predecessors you'll realize how truly blessed you are.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:43.400
Why would I ?

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:46.710
If Heinessen himself said
that to me, then I might.

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:50.160
But I don't want to hear that from someone who's sitting on his butt behind a desk in a nice safe office.

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:54.600
There shouldn't be any
major battles for a while.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.950
Enjoy your vacation
for the time being.

00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:08.430
Lieutenant, eh ?

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:11.850
It was only six hours, there's no
way I can feel any attachment to it.

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:15.460
But if I get promoted,
my salary goes up.

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:18.830
Then I can buy more books,
so I guess I should be thankful.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:21.180
You must be
Lt. Commander Yang.

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:24.560
Ah, yes.

00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:29.410
I'm Lieutenant Goodwin from the
Military Public Relations Office.

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:34.060
I've been assigned to be of
service to you for a while.

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:39.370
Lt. Commander, you're going to be
the target of a lot of media attention.

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:44.120
The Public Affairs Office sent me to help you handle the media.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:49.900
In a way, you can think of me
as your manager or spokesman.

00:04:50.570 --> 00:04:53.040
H... handle the media ?

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:54.700
Manager ?

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:55.760
Yes.

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:56.960
Just leave it to me, sir.

00:04:57.720 --> 00:04:59.760
This comes with the
territory, I guess.{This is part of
the salary, I guess.}

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:00.840
Huh ?

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:02.090
What was that, sir ?

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:05.060
N...no, it's nothing.

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:08.630
Then I probably need to brief you on your schedule of upcoming events.

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:14.160
Tomorrow, at 10:00, a press interview at
the cooperative strategy headquarters.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:13.160
Well, his rank is Lieutenant.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:15.160
Until this morning, he was my superior...

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:18.060
...but now, I'm the one to
whom he has to pay respect.

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:19.210
How strange...

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:21.710
I wonder how old he is.

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:26.630
Lieutenant is only a passing point for those
who have graduated from the military academy.

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:29.570
But for those who climbed up from the bottom, it's the terminal point...

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:33.310
...that they'll reach near
the end of their service.

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:34.480
I wonder if this is fair...

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:37.740
The day after tomorrow, from 09:00...

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:39.750
W...wait a minute.

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:42.690
How far in advance is
this "schedule" booked ?

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:44.480
For a week, at least.

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:45.530
Huh ?

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:48.850
Afterwards, there have been innumerable
requests from the media for interviews.

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:52.620
How the heck can
this be a "vacation" ?

00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:56.930
These are your new quarters.

00:05:57.970 --> 00:06:01.610
We've moved your household goods
and effects here from your old quarters.

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:03.610
If you'll tell us what
you need and where...

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:06.250
...we'll make sure the furnishings are squared away for you.

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:08.020
So please just give us the
word - anything you need.

00:06:09.190 --> 00:06:11.010
It's so large.

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:13.510
These are normal quarters
for a Lt. Commander.

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:16.780
If you need a housekeeper,
we can arrange for you.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:20.270
No, thank you,
I usually eat out, so...

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:23.220
A message ?

00:06:23.890 --> 00:06:26.050
How is this number...{known}?

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:28.470
I would guess it's a
request for an interview.

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:33.620
The Public Affairs Office has already released your number here to selected members of the media.

00:06:36.010 --> 00:06:41.910
Lt. Commander Yang, this is Wilma Vancroft,
the editor of Weekly Pretty Woman Magazine.

00:06:41.910 --> 00:06:46.520
I would really like to interview you for
our series, "This Week's Nice Guy"...

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:52.600
...because the Lt. Commander is currently No. 1 on the most eligible bachelor list...

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:56.200
It's for the wrong person.

00:06:57.960 --> 00:06:59.570
You must be Lt. Commander Yang.

00:06:59.570 --> 00:07:01.500
This is the first time we've met.

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:05.830
I'm the director of
TV Heinessen, John Martin.

00:07:06.430 --> 00:07:12.100
To tell you the truth, I'd like to have you talk
with the widow of Rear Admiral Lynch on TV.

00:07:12.940 --> 00:07:16.500
It's a 60 minute program,
and we'll pay 10,000 dinars.

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:20.450
Plus, for each 1% of the
audience rating, we'll also pay...

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:27.010
How is the widow of
Rear Admiral Lynch ?

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:32.960
I don't know for sure, but it seems she
has cleared out of military housing...

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:35.270
...and returned with her
children to her parents'...

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:41.600
This is Ale TV Heinessen.

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:44.510
In our program, we decided
to change the angle...

00:07:44.510 --> 00:07:48.350
...and looked into your family history, Lt. Commander Yang.

00:07:48.350 --> 00:07:54.270
Your parents have already passed away,
but your father's first wife is still around.

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:58.390
I'd definitely like to
realize your reunion...

00:07:59.340 --> 00:08:01.700
My father's first wife, huh ?

00:08:01.700 --> 00:08:04.320
In this case, would
she be my "stepmother" ?

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:08.490
In this world there are unexpectedly very few words that actually capture the true nature of things.

00:08:08.490 --> 00:08:10.710
Does she know that
the son of the person...

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:13.700
...with whom she parted,
has become a serviceman...

00:08:13.700 --> 00:08:18.120
...and mistakenly been
turned into a "hero" ?

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:24.870
For the next ten days, Yang felt like he was in the middle of a monsoon.

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:29.700
In the chaos of his continually packed
schedule, he never got enough sleep...

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:33.060
...and couldn't stop long enough to really taste his food when eating. {because of stress}

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:39.380
Wenli. Oh, it's been
a long time, Wenli.

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:42.400
Don't you remember me ?

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:46.360
I guess it can't be helped -
you were little then.

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:50.710
I'm Andy Luclay,
your mother's cousin.

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:54.480
I met you about
ten years ago.

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:57.780
I see, thank you.

00:08:57.780 --> 00:09:00.350
I didn't realize it, but
I guess I do have relatives.

00:09:00.860 --> 00:09:05.320
It was shortly after
your mother died.

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:10.810
Your father didn't seem to
take care of you properly.

00:09:10.810 --> 00:09:12.570
Oh, don't take it
in the wrong way.

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:14.610
Of course, there were rumors
that you and your father...

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:18.440
...were polishing vases for
many hours, in silence.

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:23.220
We thought there might be an
educational problem for the child.

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:31.160
We decided among ourselves that we should
take custody of you as your mother's relatives...

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:35.410
...but before we could, your father
took you with him out into space.

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:42.110
Since we couldn't accuse your father of kidnapping his own child we lost contact like that.

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:48.090
If such a child welfare project had been
put into effect, what would I be doing now ?

00:09:48.090 --> 00:09:51.520
Would I still be present in a place
like this and doing things like this ?

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:57.240
Well, I've always had high
expectations for you since then.

00:09:57.240 --> 00:09:59.900
Yeah, you've turned out to
be exactly what I thought.

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:07.450
If he truly had high expectations for me,
I wish he had paid my tuition five years ago.

00:10:07.820 --> 00:10:10.930
Then I wouldn't have had to
go to the military academy.

00:10:11.890 --> 00:10:14.160
Then I might have gone onto an
average university's history department...

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:18.450
...and if things had gone right I wonder if perhaps I might be preparing to go to graduate school.

00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:24.810
But then, the war with the Galactic Empire
has been going on for more than 130 years.

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:30.120
About now, I could have been drafted and
sent to the front line battlefield as a soldier.

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:34.050
To say this myself is pathetic, but
considering how unathletic I am...

00:10:34.050 --> 00:10:38.170
...I could have been killed or
captured, one or the other.

00:10:39.590 --> 00:10:42.140
Oh, oh, he can't
stop smiling.

00:10:42.140 --> 00:10:45.880
A Lt. Commander at
the age of 21, huh ?

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:49.160
If a person who could expect to go no
further than Lt. Commander in his lifetime...

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:53.660
...has already been appointed to be
Lt. Commander so quickly, I guess that's it for him.

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:56.410
He's got nothing to look
forward to in the future.

00:10:56.410 --> 00:10:58.010
You're absolutely right.

00:10:58.680 --> 00:11:02.610
I'm not obsessed with promotions,
so I could care less...

00:11:02.610 --> 00:11:04.900
...but they may be right that
I'll go no further than Lt. Commander.

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:12.510
Principal Sitolet...

00:11:12.510 --> 00:11:14.510
...Vice Admiral, sir...

00:11:17.310 --> 00:11:18.690
You did a good job.

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:21.190
I was just lucky.

00:11:31.780 --> 00:11:33.310
Well, I guess it's okay.

00:11:33.310 --> 00:11:37.950
Even if I'm a "hero" in name only,
I did save people's lives, after all.

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:41.800
It's probably better than becoming a
hero by killing many enemy soldiers.

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:53.050
Finally, in October, things
around Yang quieted down.

00:12:03.590 --> 00:12:05.960
I am presently away.

00:12:05.960 --> 00:12:09.920
Please leave a
message after the tone.

00:12:11.850 --> 00:12:13.450
Yang, I know you're there.

00:12:13.450 --> 00:12:15.270
Pick up.

00:12:17.160 --> 00:12:19.370
Just as I thought,
you're there.

00:12:19.370 --> 00:12:21.370
I figured you were
pretending to be away...

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:24.510
...so you wouldn't have to deal with
the media or your newfound relatives.

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:27.320
Where are you calling from ?

00:12:27.320 --> 00:12:30.710
I thought you were on assignment,
but it sounds like you're nearby.

00:12:31.510 --> 00:12:33.950
I'm here on Heinessen
for some errands.

00:12:34.410 --> 00:12:35.510
Shall we meet ?

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:41.020
I'm sorry, but I've got only 30
minutes - it'll be like a flip-flop.

00:12:41.020 --> 00:12:45.430
We've been missing each other like this all
this year, since both of us have been busy.

00:12:45.430 --> 00:12:48.040
Though I've finally gotten some time off.

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:49.940
You're between assignments ?

00:12:49.940 --> 00:12:54.540
I'm envious that you're getting
paid without doing anything.

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:56.560
It's not hectic...

00:12:56.560 --> 00:12:59.750
...though I'm a little apprehensive about
where I'll be sent on my next assignment.

00:13:00.260 --> 00:13:02.840
Well, there's no point
in worrying about it.

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:06.390
In any case, you're
the Hero of El Facil.

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:11.160
They won't send you to a place where
you could die easily, for their own sake.

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:16.270
You don't seem to enjoy
being called a "hero."

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:20.600
But you're the fastest
to be promoted in our class.

00:13:20.600 --> 00:13:21.930
I've got high hopes for you.

00:13:22.520 --> 00:13:25.200
I don't plan on being promoted
for another ten years.

00:13:26.430 --> 00:13:28.100
I'll look forward
to it in ten years.

00:13:29.060 --> 00:13:30.330
Ten years from now, eh ?

00:13:31.050 --> 00:13:35.190
I sometimes think that servicemen's
promotions are like mountain climbing.

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:36.320
Mountain climbing ?

00:13:36.320 --> 00:13:43.060
To keep climbing a thin, steep path,
or to fall down to the bottom of the valley...

00:13:43.060 --> 00:13:44.910
...I wonder which
is more desirable ?

00:13:44.910 --> 00:13:46.810
You've gotten so melancholy.

00:13:46.810 --> 00:13:48.510
You've succeeded
and you're still like this.

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:50.760
I wonder how depressed you
would have been if you had failed.

00:13:52.510 --> 00:13:54.970
Oh, it's time to go.

00:13:54.970 --> 00:13:57.430
Next time around, I want
to meet up, all three of us.

00:13:59.660 --> 00:14:00.800
Yeah, definitely.

00:14:01.550 --> 00:14:02.240
Bye.

00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:11.630
I've truly gotten melancholy.

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:16.260
I wonder what I'll be
doing ten years from now ?

00:14:17.010 --> 00:14:21.760
No, if you're in the military, there's
no guarantee you'll even be alive.

00:14:21.760 --> 00:14:23.710
Well, assuming I stay alive...

00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:26.290
...considering the way I am, there
won't be anyone who'll marry me...

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:29.810
...so I'll probably still be living
the same military life as now.

00:14:29.810 --> 00:14:34.430
And if nothing bad happens, the long
retirement life will be waiting for me...

00:14:35.150 --> 00:14:37.760
Come to think of it, retired
servicemen tend to live long...

00:14:37.760 --> 00:14:43.150
...because they've led a well-regulated,
healthy life since their youth.

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:46.110
I guess I'd be one of those long-living old men
who gives trouble to whoever is around him...

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:51.960
...and constantly complains about young
people and is avoided by people around him.

00:14:53.310 --> 00:14:55.780
I'm presently away.

00:14:55.780 --> 00:14:59.710
Please leave a
message at the tone.

00:15:01.660 --> 00:15:04.290
Yang, I know you're there.

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:05.880
Give it up and
pick up the phone.

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:09.700
You've probably got idle hands,
just thinking about insignificant things.

00:15:10.520 --> 00:15:11.990
Why does everyone know that ?

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:15.370
You're there,
just as I thought.

00:15:15.370 --> 00:15:16.720
Of course I am.

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:18.140
I'm supposed to be awaiting orders.

00:15:18.830 --> 00:15:21.610
Is the media
still bugging you ?

00:15:22.410 --> 00:15:24.150
Yes, kinda.

00:15:24.150 --> 00:15:27.880
In any case, you shouldn't
be such a shut in.

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:30.000
Come to my office tomorrow.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:31.680
I have a job for you.

00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:33.460
A job ?

00:15:33.460 --> 00:15:36.190
Yes, a new
assignment for the hero.

00:15:40.760 --> 00:15:44.020
Commander Alex Cazellnu
was 27 years old at the time.

00:15:44.020 --> 00:15:48.380
He's a top brain who published a dissertation on systems engineering while he was still in school...

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:52.460
...and was scouted by executives
from large corporations.

00:15:53.150 --> 00:15:55.620
He's a military bureaucrat with an
expertise in supply and rear-line support...

00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:57.970
...and was said to
have a bright future.

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:02.570
But since he is uncompromising
with a sharp tongue...

00:16:02.570 --> 00:16:05.610
...he's not well liked among some
authoritarian top ranking officials.

00:16:06.300 --> 00:16:10.670
On the other hand, he's easy going and takes good care of his juniors, so he's quite popular among them.

00:16:11.560 --> 00:16:14.840
For Yang, Cazellnu was a senior to whom he was very indebted;

00:16:14.840 --> 00:16:17.830
Cazellnu served as a young chief
secretary at the military school...

00:16:17.830 --> 00:16:20.820
...while Yang was still a student and
he {i.e. Cazellnu} helped him along during that time.

00:16:22.450 --> 00:16:29.810
You always say you want to retire but shall
I predict your future for you if you quit right now ?

00:16:29.810 --> 00:16:30.990
Huh ?

00:16:30.990 --> 00:16:36.260
Most likely, you'll be wanted by many
corporations for publicity purposes.

00:16:36.260 --> 00:16:42.950
Taking a pretty woman's hand, you'll say on the
TV screen, "This is the ultimate tea I've chosen !"

00:16:43.430 --> 00:16:44.380
Huh ?

00:16:44.380 --> 00:16:47.150
Then you'll be dragged
into an election in no time.

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:49.590
I'll take a guess: you'll
gather about 3,000,000 votes.

00:16:49.590 --> 00:16:54.250
There are some children among them, but
you've got a large following of relatives...

00:16:54.250 --> 00:16:59.520
...and you're the new star with bright future who can get a large number of votes from the start.

00:16:59.520 --> 00:17:01.890
Each and every party and clique
will want you and pester you...

00:17:01.890 --> 00:17:05.420
...and then leave you in the
morass of political warfare.

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:11.860
You might not like it, but it is also a
fact that this military organization...

00:17:11.860 --> 00:17:16.740
...is in some ways shielding you from
a merciless, competitive society.

00:17:18.420 --> 00:17:19.660
In any case...

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:23.630
...one thing that's for sure is that you're not
qualified to receive a retirement pension...

00:17:23.630 --> 00:17:27.120
...because you haven't yet
spent ten years in the force.

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:31.820
Even if we count from your enrollment at the
military academy, it's only been five years.

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:35.370
At the very least, you'll have to
bear with it for another five years.

00:17:35.370 --> 00:17:39.090
Until then, you'll have to be prepared
to be penniless if you quit the force.

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:42.600
Oh yeah, I met Jean
Robert Lap yesterday.

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:46.760
He said you were
the pride of the class.

00:17:46.760 --> 00:17:49.180
It's the other way around, the one who
says it and the one whom it is said about.

00:17:49.180 --> 00:17:50.460
Don't be so humble.

00:17:50.460 --> 00:17:52.850
No, I actually mean it.

00:17:52.850 --> 00:17:57.420
I personally think that the one
who'll get promoted the most is Lap.

00:17:58.560 --> 00:18:01.020
The valedictorian was
Wideborn, wasn't it ?

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:09.160
Wideborn tends to be too logical, and he also
has a tendency to censure people's faults...

00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:12.750
...so he wasn't very well liked by his classmates or lower classmen.

00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:15.870
In the long term,
Lap will come out on top.

00:18:15.870 --> 00:18:17.130
In the long term ?

00:18:17.130 --> 00:18:20.980
In the capacity of a commander,
leading other people, I mean.

00:18:20.980 --> 00:18:22.100
I see.

00:18:22.100 --> 00:18:25.400
The trustworthy and magnetic
personality, I suppose.

00:18:25.400 --> 00:18:28.510
By the way, aside from
the respected Lap...

00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:33.710
I assume you know who
Fleet Admiral Bruce Ashbey is ?

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:38.160
I'm offended that you
think I'm so ignorant.

00:18:38.160 --> 00:18:41.660
43 years ago, he led
the 2nd battle of Tiamat...

00:18:41.660 --> 00:18:45.710
...where he led the Alliance to a lopsided
victory, and then died during the battle.

00:18:45.710 --> 00:18:50.000
He's said to be the most famed hero in
the history of the Free Planets Alliance forces.

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:52.090
I see you're
good at history.

00:18:52.090 --> 00:18:55.710
Well, I guess we all have at
least one thing we're good at.

00:18:55.710 --> 00:18:58.590
And what about Admiral Ashbey ?

00:18:58.590 --> 00:19:01.100
There's someone who asserts
that he didn't die in battle.

00:19:02.040 --> 00:19:03.840
If he didn't die in
battle, what happened ?

00:19:03.840 --> 00:19:04.920
Murder.

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:12.330
Well, it's something that
we can't just ignore, right ?

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:14.610
History is filled with
conflicting theories.

00:19:14.610 --> 00:19:15.320
Yes.

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:19.410
And this is one theory that
the military can't ignore.

00:19:19.410 --> 00:19:22.340
In regards to the nature of
Fleet Admiral Ashbey's death...

00:19:22.340 --> 00:19:25.990
...it's already an established
historical fact, isn't it ?

00:19:25.990 --> 00:19:28.320
Is there any reason that
it's being challenged now ?

00:19:28.960 --> 00:19:30.230
The reason is...

00:19:38.140 --> 00:19:40.440
Lieutenant Minci,
bring me that file.

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:48.160
Fleet Admiral Bruce Ashbey is number
one in the history of the Alliance Fleet...

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:50.470
...in terms of his
accomplishments and fame.

00:19:50.470 --> 00:19:55.730
He died in battle in 745 at the age of 35,
but his title at the time was Admiral.

00:19:55.730 --> 00:19:58.530
He was promoted to Fleet
Admiral upon his death...

00:19:58.530 --> 00:20:01.960
...and that was the record for the youngest
Fleet Admiral in the Alliance Fleet.

00:20:02.510 --> 00:20:06.700
Not only did he lead the Alliance Force to a
lopsided victory in the 2nd battle of Tiamat...

00:20:06.700 --> 00:20:09.160
...but he also won
each battle he fought.

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:09.690
Thank you.

00:20:11.090 --> 00:20:14.500
Those renowned commanders with
fame equal to him in our history are...

00:20:14.500 --> 00:20:20.590
...the fleet admirals of the Battle of
Dagon Starzone, Limpao and Yusuf Tparl.

00:20:21.150 --> 00:20:27.330
Anyway, the starting point of this incident is that there was a letter sent to military HQ.

00:20:27.840 --> 00:20:30.760
In the past 36 weeks,
there have been 36 letters.

00:20:30.760 --> 00:20:35.150
Since they're delivered every Tuesday, we've
called them the "Tuesday correspondence."

00:20:36.190 --> 00:20:38.870
"Bruce Ashbey was murdered."

00:20:38.870 --> 00:20:41.640
All 36 letters had
the same content.

00:20:41.860 --> 00:20:42.890
Is this everything ?

00:20:42.890 --> 00:20:44.100
That's it.

00:20:44.360 --> 00:20:48.470
But there must be some meaning
behind the repeated letters.

00:20:48.470 --> 00:20:52.450
So Headquarters decided
to settle the formalities.

00:20:52.450 --> 00:20:54.440
"To settle the formalities" ?

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:55.410
In other words...

00:20:55.410 --> 00:20:58.860
...the objective is to prove that Bruce Ashbey's
death is definitively a death in battle...

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:03.820
...and that there's no possibility
that it was murder.

00:21:03.820 --> 00:21:06.990
But it's not like these
offer any proof, do they ?

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:09.150
Why don't we
just ignore them ?

00:21:09.150 --> 00:21:13.020
If we ignore them, the
embers will always remain.

00:21:13.020 --> 00:21:17.160
And for us to know whether or not it has
any basis in fact, we have to investigate.

00:21:17.160 --> 00:21:19.310
Ah, yes, you're right, but...

00:21:19.310 --> 00:21:22.160
So the new Lt. Commander, Yang Wenli...

00:21:22.160 --> 00:21:25.570
...has been informally appointed to
be in charge of the investigation.

00:21:25.570 --> 00:21:27.540
I'm supposed to do it ?

00:21:27.540 --> 00:21:30.920
Why would I give you all
this explanation otherwise ?

00:21:30.920 --> 00:21:32.570
Why me ?

00:21:32.570 --> 00:21:34.950
You've been inconvenienced
by too much time off, right ?

00:21:34.950 --> 00:21:37.160
I've never once been inconvenienced
by too much time off.

00:21:38.160 --> 00:21:42.230
It hasn't been decided whether or not a
formal investigation committee will be formed.

00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:47.460
Basically, that decision will depend on your
findings, to form or not form the committee.

00:21:47.460 --> 00:21:49.090
Okay, sure.

00:21:49.090 --> 00:21:50.760
You don't sound
very enthusiastic.

00:21:51.760 --> 00:21:54.140
I actually am not
very enthusiastic.

00:21:54.140 --> 00:21:57.470
I'm sorry, but I have
to be very blunt about it.{not to have the
content, lid, or the bottom.}

00:21:57.470 --> 00:21:59.310
Yang...{Yang}

00:21:59.310 --> 00:22:03.160
I mean, this is just a part of
information regulation, isn't it ?

00:22:03.160 --> 00:22:06.560
The fame of heroes is the
pride of the military forces.

00:22:06.560 --> 00:22:11.210
What top officials really want is the legend, not the truth, right ?

00:22:12.160 --> 00:22:17.210
If some inconvenient fact crops up,
I'm sure they'll either hide or destroy it.

00:22:17.210 --> 00:22:20.160
I don't want to do a pre-investigation
for something like that.

00:22:20.160 --> 00:22:23.160
Moreover, I wouldn't want
to be held responsible...

00:22:23.160 --> 00:22:26.050
...when such a scheme by
the military comes to light.

00:22:28.180 --> 00:22:30.430
You don't have to think
that deeply about it.

00:22:30.430 --> 00:22:31.900
Then what ?

00:22:32.410 --> 00:22:34.020
It's a moratorium.

00:22:34.710 --> 00:22:37.430
You've accomplished too much.

00:22:37.430 --> 00:22:41.750
So your new assignment won't
be decided any time soon.

00:22:41.750 --> 00:22:43.950
It'll take time for each department
to make personnel decisions.

00:22:44.760 --> 00:22:45.860
So ?

00:22:45.860 --> 00:22:52.260
If I give you some sort of a job,
it'll be beneficial in several ways.

00:22:52.990 --> 00:22:56.160
You can shut out the noise from the
outside and it's the type of a job...

00:22:56.160 --> 00:22:58.160
...that you can
pretty much suspend...

00:22:58.160 --> 00:23:01.880
...if you formally receive your
next assignment in the meantime.

00:23:08.760 --> 00:23:12.830
Besides, if you show some competence
in this area and prove your talent...

00:23:12.830 --> 00:23:18.010
...you might be recruited to be a researcher
in the War History Compilation Institute.

00:23:18.670 --> 00:23:21.570
Do you actually think so ?

00:23:21.570 --> 00:23:24.400
No, actually, this is just
some bait to tempt you.

00:23:25.020 --> 00:23:26.730
I see.

00:23:27.970 --> 00:23:30.420
This is what I mean by
not being very enthusiastic.

00:23:31.130 --> 00:23:32.950
Hey, don't say that.

00:23:32.950 --> 00:23:37.380
Besides, you might be feeling ashamed about
being fed forever without doing anything.

00:23:37.380 --> 00:23:40.410
For the sake of your mental
health, do some work.

00:24:11.740 --> 00:24:12.780
I understand.

00:24:12.780 --> 00:24:13.730
I'll take the job.

00:24:18.010 --> 00:24:22.090
Yang Wenli's personality was very
much enriched with flexibility.

00:24:22.090 --> 00:24:25.760
It might be because he had always
had to adapt to the changes of fate...

00:24:25.760 --> 00:24:27.690
...and circumstances
since he was a child.

00:24:27.690 --> 00:24:32.820
Whether or not that has strengthened
or weakened his character...

00:24:33.740 --> 00:24:36.160
...is hard to
tell at this point.

00:24:36.860 --> 00:24:41.050
It's not like I can live
forever doing nothing.

00:24:41.050 --> 00:24:42.470
Well, I have no choice.

00:24:43.270 --> 00:24:46.610
In any case, Yang's new
job has been determined:

00:24:46.610 --> 00:24:50.140
The investigation of Fleet Admiral
Bruce Ashbey's murder hypothesis.

00:24:51.060 --> 00:24:53.910
That this assignment, which initially
seems to be very much insignificant...

00:24:53.910 --> 00:24:58.760
...would lead Yang into a new
happening was something no one knew.

00:24:57.260 --> 00:25:04.810
The Hero's New Assignment

00:25:05.500 --> 00:25:10.450
Preview of Next Episode

00:25:09.330 --> 00:25:11.250
Being assigned to a
task against his will...

00:25:11.250 --> 00:25:14.250
...Yang initially started by investigating
the public records of the past.

00:25:14.250 --> 00:25:18.040
Those were about the accomplishments
of Fleet Admiral Bruce Ashbey...

00:25:18.040 --> 00:25:22.290
...and his allies called
the "Year 730 Mafia."

00:25:23.010 --> 00:25:25.510
Next episode of Legend of the
Galactic Heroes Gaiden, Spiral Labyrinth...

00:25:25.580 --> 00:25:35.550
Legend of the Galactic Heroes Gaiden Spiral Labyrinth
Chapter 3

00:25:25.580 --> 00:25:35.550
The Profiles of Heroes

00:25:29.750 --> 00:25:33.810
Humans create history,
and retell history.
